    "section_evoo_v3_faq_rRJhLR": {
      "type": "section-evoo-v3-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_wg78Aq": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How is AIWO Taurine different from the taurine in energy drinks?",
            "answer": "<p>Energy drinks contain taurine but in small, unstandardised amounts alongside caffeine, sugar, and artificial additives that confound any individual benefit. AIWO Taurine is pure amino acid powder with no stimulants, no sugar, no flavours. You control the dose. You can use it consistently. That's what clinical research studies not energy drink formulations.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_BFc6Am": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does Taurine actually do?",
            "answer": "<p>Taurine is the most abundant free amino acid in the heart. It supports cardiac muscle contraction, regulates cellular calcium balance, and has been studied in multiple RCTs for its role in blood pressure support, exercise recovery, and antioxidant defence in cardiac and skeletal tissue. In the brain, it supports GABA receptor activity the inhibitory pathway that promotes calm and regulates stress responsiveness.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_pgG9dR": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who benefits most from AIWO Taurine?",
            "answer": "<p>Adults with cardiovascular risk awareness (elevated blood pressure, cholesterol), individuals under high chronic stress, regular exercisers seeking recovery support, or anyone building a metabolic longevity protocol. Taurine depletion increases with age making consistent supplementation particularly relevant from age 35 onwards. Consult your physician before use if on blood pressure or cardiac medication.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_zet6LP": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is AIWO Taurine vegan?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — taurine can be produced synthetically from plant-derived precursors with no animal involvement. AIWO Taurine is unflavoured pure powder. Verify certification status from current label before using the vegan badge in consumer copy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Q6TUxh": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long before I notice a difference?",
            "answer": "<p>Clinical studies on taurine and blood pressure outcomes used supplementation periods of 2 to 12 weeks. Cardiovascular and metabolic support builds with consistent daily use. A 60–90 day benchmark with AIWO 181 biomarker tracking including blood pressure, CRP, and relevant cardiac markers is a practical way to measure individual response. Individual results vary.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
